APT - package manager
Usage: apt <action> [package]

Actions:
  list                 list available packages
  installed            list installed packages
  search <t>           search name and description
  info <pkg>           show package metadata
  depends <pkg>        show install order (dependencies first)
  sources              list configured repositories
  add-source <kind> <location>
                       add a repository ('local <dir>' or 'net <url>')
  remove-source <url>  drop a repository
  update               refresh package lists from sources
  upgrade              install newer versions of installed packages
  install <pkg>        install a package and its dependencies
  remove <pkg>         remove a package
  autoremove           remove unneeded automatic dependencies
  verify               check installed files against recorded checksums

Examples:
  apt add-source net https://example.com/cloveros/
  apt update
  apt install remotetool

Repository formats:
  local <dir>   a directory of <name>/package.lua plus a payload
  net   <url>   serves index.lua (a serialized table of package metadata)
                and <name>/<file> for each file in a package

Integrity:
  A network repository may publish a sha256 digest per file in its index.
  When it does, a file whose bytes do not match is refused and nothing is
  written. A package with no published digest installs but is listed as
  [unverified] by 'apt installed', so it is never mistaken for a verified
  one.

Notes:
  Repositories are stored in etc/apt/sources.list; 'apt sources' and
  'apt add-source' edit that file.
  'apt update' reports any repository it could not reach, and exits
  non-zero when it could not read at least one index.
